chunk-lens — Prior Art and Attribution
=======================================

This project is an independent implementation. No source code was copied from
any other project. The following prior art informed what features to build and
which defects to fix.

ChunkViz v0.1
  Author:  Greg Kamradt
  URL:     https://chunkviz.up.railway.app
  Source:  https://github.com/gkamradt/ChunkViz
  License: MIT
  Notes:   Inspired the core visualization concept (continuous text block with
           background colour runs). chunk-lens corrects the character-count
           statistic, enables overlap on all strategies, adds gap rendering,
           and improves accessibility.

LangChain text splitters
  URL:     https://python.langchain.com/docs/modules/data_connection/document_transformers/
  Notes:   The separator ladders used in the recursive strategies are the
           LangChain standard sets (plain-text, JavaScript, Python, Markdown).
           They are the de-facto reference; identical ladders allow direct
           comparison with LangChain outputs. See src/lib/splitters/separators.ts.

Llama Index text splitters
  URL:     https://docs.llamaindex.ai/en/stable/api_reference/node_parsers/
  Notes:   Referenced for understanding sentence-splitting behaviour and
           markdown-header strategy semantics.
